cel\u00a0or Netlify for React and frontend projects, GitHub Pages for static HTML\/CSS\/JS sites, and Render or Railway for backend Node.js projects. All offer free tiers that are more than enough for portfolio projects.","inLanguage":"en-US"},"inLanguage":"en-US"},{"@type":"Question","@id":"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/web-development-projects\/#faq-question-1783399943378","position":6,"url":"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/web-development-projects\/#faq-question-1783399943378","name":"6. Which web development projects are best for learning backend development?","answerCount":1,"acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Authentication in Node.js, Link Shortener, and Real-Time Chat App are the best projects for learning backend. They cover databases, REST APIs, session management, and real-time communication, which are the core pillars of backend development.","inLanguage":"en-US"},"inLanguage":"en-US"},{"@type":"Question","@id":"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/web-development-projects\/#faq-question-1783399954756","position":7,"url":"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/web-development-projects\/#faq-question-1783399954756","name":"7. How long does it take to complete a web development project?","answerCount":1,"acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"A beginner-level project like a to-do list or landing page takes 2 to 4 days. An intermediate project like\u00a0a\u00a0quiz app takes 1 to 2 weeks. A full-stack project like an e-commerce website can take 3 to\u00a06 weeks\u00a0depending on how many features you build.","inLanguage":"en-US"},"inLanguage":"en-US"},{"@type":"Question","@id":"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/web-development-projects\/#faq-question-1783399972986","position":8,"url":"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/web-development-projects\/#faq-question-1783399972986","name":"8. What web development projects should final year students build?","answerCount":1,"acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Final year students should build at least one full-stack project such as an e-commerce site, social media clone, or job board. These show depth, handle real-world complexity, and give you a lot to discuss in interviews. Add a deployment link and a clean README to each project.","inLanguage":"en-US"},"inLanguage":"en-US"},{"@type":"Question","@id":"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/web-development-projects\/#faq-question-1783399991139","position":9,"url":"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/web-development-projects\/#faq-question-1783399991139","name":"9. Do I need to know React to start web development projects?","answerCount":1,"acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No. Many beginner projects in this list use only HTML, CSS, and Vanilla JavaScript. Learn\u00a0React\u00a0after you are comfortable with the basics. Projects like the to-do list, background generator, and landing page do not require React at all.","inLanguage":"en-US"},"inLanguage":"en-US"},{"@type":"Question","@id":"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/web-development-projects\/#faq-question-1783400027408","position":10,"url":"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/web-development-projects\/#faq-question-1783400027408","name":"10. How do I make my web development projects stand out to recruiters?","answerCount":1,"acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Deploy your project with a live URL, write a clear README explaining what the project does and how to run it, and add screenshots or a short demo video. Recruiters spend\u00a0very little\u00a0time on each application, so make it as easy as possible for them to see your work\u00a0immediately.","inLanguage":"en-US"},"inLanguage":"en-US"}]}},"_links":{"self":[{"href":"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/posts\/5103","targetHints":{"allow":["GET"]}}],"collection":[{"href":"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/posts"}],"about":[{"href":"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/types\/post"}],"author":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/www